{%- comment -%} Renders the shop logo image or the shop name as a serif wordmark. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- if settings.logo != blank -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign logo_2x = settings.logo_width | times: 2
    assign logo_alt = shop.name | escape
    assign logo_style = '--logo-width: ' | append: settings.logo_width | append: 'px;'
    assign logo_sizes = settings.logo_width | append: 'px'
  -%}
  <a class="header__logo" href="{{ routes.root_url }}" aria-label="{{ shop.name | escape }}">
    {{
      settings.logo
      | image_url: width: logo_2x
      | image_tag:
        loading: 'eager',
        fetchpriority: 'high',
        widths: '120, 160, 200, 240, 320, 480, 640',
        sizes: logo_sizes,
        alt: logo_alt,
        style: logo_style
    }}
  </a>
{%- else -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    The text wordmark has to fit a sidebar that can be as narrow as 180px, in
    any heading font, cased or uppercased by the preset. The longest word decides
    how small it may need to get (a multi-word name can still wrap between
    words); header.liquid caps the size against the column width with it, and
    theme.js trims further only if an unusually wide font still overflows.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign logo_chars = 1
    assign logo_words = shop.name | split: ' '
    for logo_word in logo_words
      if logo_word.size > logo_chars
        assign logo_chars = logo_word.size
      endif
    endfor
  -%}
  <a class="header__logo" href="{{ routes.root_url }}">
    <span class="header__logo-text" style="--logo-chars: {{ logo_chars }};" data-logo-fit>{{ shop.name | escape }}</span>
  </a>
{%- endif -%}
